<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h1 class="display-4 fw-bold mb-3">Contract Management</h1>
        <p class="lead mb-4">
            Protect your project margins and legal position with structured administration of client and vendor 
            contracts within standardized industry frameworks.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Lifecycle Contract Administration</h2>
        <p>
            The contracts module supports lifecycle administration from inception through to the final account 
            release. Standard libraries for FIDIC and NEC contract conditions provide the framework for professional 
            site administration, with configurable templates for various procurement models including lump sum, 
            re-measure, and cost-plus contracts.
        </p>
        <p>
            Centralized contract registers track key dates for mobilization, practical completion, and the 
            defects liability period. Automated notifications alert project executives when critical 
            timelines for contractual notices are approaching, preventing the loss of rights due to 
            administrative oversight.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Variation Order (VO) Management</h2>
        <p>
            Control the impact of changes with a rigorous variation order workflow. Every change to the 
            original scope is tracked from initial discovery through to formal valuation and client 
            approval. By linking VOs directly to budget cost codes and schedule activities, the system 
            provides immediate visibility into how technical changes impact the commercial bottom line.
        </p>
        <p>
            Historical VO logs provide essential data for final account negotiations and claim analysis, 
            ensuring that every additional work performed on site is captured and remunerated 
            according to the contract's valuation principles.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Correspondence and Claims History</h2>
        <p>
            Integrated correspondence logs maintain an immutable record of all project-related letters, site 
            instructions, notices, and claims. In the event of a dispute, this centralized history 
            provides the "contemporaneous records" required by project auditors and legal counsel 
            to protect the organization's interests.
        </p>
        <p>
            A dedicated dispute and claim register tracks the status of contested items through resolution, 
            providing a dashboard view of commercial exposure across the portfolio. This transparency 
            enables proactive dispute management and informed provisioning for potential project 
            liabilities.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

